# Final Principle

Powerful punches are not created by stronger arms.

They emerge from a coordinated kinetic chain,

where the legs generate force,

the trunk transfers it,

and the upper limb delivers it efficiently.

The Cable Punch develops this chain under controlled resistance,

bridging strength training and combat performance.